{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/competency_course_cm

    One linked activity's extras on the course competencies page, beside core's link to it: what completing it does
    for the competency (its outcome, as core names it, read-only here: it is edited in the activity's settings), and,
    for a learner, whether they completed it. Drawn into data-region="dim-comp-cm" by the theme's copy of
    tool_lp/course_competencies_page on the first paint, and on the client by theme_dimensions/coursecompetencies
    after core re-renders the page. The outcome is a status label in the tone the server picked from a fixed list
    (neutral, rated, status, proficient: the dim-comp-pill modifiers); the label's meaning is its words.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cmid - the activity
    * outcomename, outcometone - core's name of the outcome and its tone
    * hasstate, isdone, istodo - the learner's state; statetext - it as a sentence

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cmid": 31,
        "outcome": 1,
        "outcomename": "Attach evidence",
        "outcometone": "rated",
        "hasstate": true,
        "isdone": true,
        "istodo": false,
        "statetext": "Completed on 2 October 2026"
    }
}}
<span class="dim-comp-course-cm">
    <span class="dim-comp-pill dim-comp-pill--{{outcometone}}"><span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}} competency_coursecmoutcome, theme_dimensions {{/str}} </span>{{outcomename}}</span>
    {{#hasstate}}
    <span class="dim-comp-course-cmstate{{#isdone}} dim-comp-course-cmstate--done{{/isdone}}">
        {{#isdone}}<i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/isdone}}
        {{#istodo}}<i class="fa-regular fa-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/istodo}}
        <span>{{statetext}}</span>
    </span>
    {{/hasstate}}
</span>
